{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1323785-sphere-system","id":1323785,"title":"Sphere System","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-07-11T15:02:54-07:00","id":1323785,"title":"Sphere System","content":"Just curious as to how many people here actually enjoy using Mage's open toolkit. Do most here view it as a genuine pleasure or something that's a necessary evil when playing a Mage game? How does it stack up against the more defined parameters of disciplines, Gifts, and hedge sorcery? Do you find it easier or more convenient to use? I've read a lot of Mage fluff to be sure, but have never played a game with a system like this before; and in truth am a little intimidated by not having firmer guidelines in place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23641-tacotuesday","name":"TacoTuesday","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T21:13:52-07:00","id":1323854,"title":"","content":"It's the reason I play Mage, the openness of Magick. Hedge Sorcery is cool but being able to control any element as opposed to say, fire from Hellfire (Without spending 800 exp on learning other paths), is a freeness I like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T22:13:55-07:00","id":1323860,"title":"","content":"I love it, but like any open/flexible system, who you're playing with matters a lot to enjoying it. If people aren't on the same page, it can really mess with how people react to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T23:22:51-07:00","id":1323871,"title":"","content":"I enjoy it, it has issues but I enjoy it. And different writers and authorities seem to differ on their interpretations and sensibilities though.<br /> <br /> I do wish they would address Archsphere in M20.<br /> <br /> And I would enjoy it, a pipe dream, to have some throw back Masters and Archmages who use Foundations, or some with unique spheres, like thematic spheres mentioned in the Storyteller's Handbook like a Fire Sphere that represents flame and passion and fire spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T23:55:44-07:00","id":1323878,"title":"","content":"I've been coming up with a Death Sphere (Influenced by the Sphere I saw on here a while back) for a while now but so far I only have 1 dot of it done, it works well enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T00:24:15-07:00","id":1323881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jihelu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1323785-sphere-system?p=1323878#post1323878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been coming up with a Death Sphere (Influenced by the Sphere I saw on here a while back) for a while now but so far I only have 1 dot of it done, it works well enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well lets see it! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T01:54:17-07:00","id":1323889,"title":"","content":"If you're going to add Death, why not just port over Awakening's Arcana?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T03:51:46-07:00","id":1323906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TacoTuesday</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1323785-sphere-system#post1323785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just curious as to how many people here actually enjoy using Mage's open toolkit. Do most here view it as a genuine pleasure or something that's a necessary evil when playing a Mage game?</div> </div> </div> </div>I absolutely *love* it. To this day I'm impressed that a system that pretty much allows you to come up with any kind of magical effect imaginable, while also encompassing pretty much every aspect of reality around us, was implemented in such a relatively simple manner. Even if it *seems* complex.<br /> <br /> It it very confusing at first? Yes, especially since it's so out of the ordinary for most game systems with strict 'spells'. Does its flexibility mean that you have edge cases piled on houserules piled on a lack of handholding? Yes. Because it is impossible to make a rule for everything, in a system with infinite possibilities.<br /> <br /> But that's pretty much the price to pay for a system that lets you do everything, and over time you develop a very good sense and feel for it; It loses its daunting percieved complexity and becomes something surprisingly simple to use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T05:19:42-07:00","id":1323922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1323785-sphere-system?p=1323860#post1323860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love it, but like any open/flexible system, who you're playing with matters a lot to enjoying it. If people aren't on the same page, it can really mess with how people react to it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Pretty much this.<br /> <br /> I find it easy to use, and very satisfying too. It feels good to be able to invent new powers when you need them, being constrained more by your imagination than a set of specific RAW within the context of your power.<br /> <br /> But much of this does depend of the group dynamics. The system requires interpretation, and it's boud to generate different opinions on how things work. It's a good idea, thus, to respect the ST opinion and not start arguments about the system in game. It also requires the ST trusting players and trying to not shut down ideas. What you're really going to be able to do with your character depends greatly on these interpretations and attitudes.<br /> <br /> I'm also of the opinion that Mage <i>requires </i>to be house ruled. An ST that's constantly trying to respect hard RAW it's going to limit greatly what the system <i>insinuates </i>you should be able to do. But this is also an aspect of the group social contract","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T06:48:41-07:00","id":1323945,"title":"","content":"While i love the Sphere system for it's openness and freeform aspects i must say that i hate the &quot;purple paradigm&quot;.<br /> Every single game i've either played in or STd i've seen players uttering the sentence &quot;but he can do it, and we have the same dots&quot;. Just because you have the same dot's it doesn't mean you can do the same thing in the same way. Paradigm, upbringing, Tradition, all these things influence how your character views magick and what they think is possible to do with the dots they have.<br /> I personally prefer the Foundation and pillar system (even if i think it could use a revision) as it somewhat keeps the openness of the sphere system but each &quot;Tradition&quot; is limited by their 4 Pillars, which are specially crafted to deal with that particular mages world-view and paradigm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T10:26:25-07:00","id":1323995,"title":"","content":"Mage's sphere system is a very interesting concept. On one hand it allows the players to cast various effects and they don't always have to care about &quot;what spell does my mage actually know?&quot; you can just wing it. On the other hand, it can be a tough challenge for a storyteller to design genuine Mage NPCs who have a casting style that feels unique or even &quot;not standard&quot;.<br /> <br /> Early game Mage plays very much like most other WoD games. Mid game is when the game begins breaking the conventions of normal storytelling. There is a quote from Awakenings &quot;Imperial Mysteries&quot; regarding a high level playstile. It states that with becoming Archmages the characters no longer had to think about &quot;how&quot; to do things but rather &quot;if&quot; they should do it. This is even more true in Mage. Depending on how you and your party handles things like rituals or rotes, from the 4th dot of Arete and onwards the normal playstile will break down and the ST will have to think out of the box and in very interesting new ways.<br /> &quot;We don't have to storm into the building. I can just awaken it's spirit and ask it to kill everyone inside.&quot; &lt;- This could be a solution the players (or their characters) can come up with. So instead of a dungeon crawl you'll have a visit to the umbral reflection of the spirit and a challenge to coerce the spirit to listen to your request.<br /> <br /> The system also depends strongly on the players willingness to limit their characters powers! That's what the paradigm can do. It's why you should only have one praxis, even though you can make your own one if you really want to. Every characters has their own way of seeing the world and while two mages may have the same sphere dots and basically cast the same spell the consequences can (and should) differ! That's a challenge for players and storytellers alike.<br /> I tend to be very serious about the metaphysics of Mage. For me, that's the main selling point of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13221-thevarulfen","name":"TheVarulfen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T11:43:26-07:00","id":1324015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1323785-sphere-system?p=1323889#post1323889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're going to add Death, why not just port over Awakening's Arcana?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Death Arcana in Awakening tends to do more stuff earlier than what you would expect in M20. I think like, Death 2 lets you do something that would be something like spirit 3 in Ascension so I've dumbed it all down a bit. (I did steal from Awakening a bit for inspiration though)<br /> <br /> Here's what I've got so far. <a href=\"https://1drv.ms/w/s!AlFDKQ1Lqjr_v21-tTxCDaAiBC15\" target=\"_blank\">https://1drv.ms/w/s!AlFDKQ1Lqjr_v21-tTxCDaAiBC15</a><br /> I appreciate comments/concerns if you got them. Thinking death 2 is basically spirit 2 for all purposes, but with wraiths. Was intending on letting Death 3 have a 'fear attack' that invokes the fear of death into people and can get them to flee, was also going to give it the ability to damage, or heal, wraiths like Entropy 3 (Without Prime 2, not sure the fuck where that comes from). Death 4 I intended on letting attack Vampires, not fully dead or alive but close enough to dead, and Death 5 would be able to flat out hurt humans (Making it the worse damage in the game sphere wise but I was going to make it unsoakable Agg to compensate a bit)<br /> <br /> Example rotes I had in mind:<br /> Death 3 Life 3, make your body dead like a vampires but still living to soak like a vampire<br /> <br /> Death 5/Life 3 (Or 4), temporarily make your body dead like a Lich, only agg can kill you for the duration. <br /> <br /> Originally I was going to call this the 'necromancy' sphere but I view necromancy as one part life one part death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T11:56:14-07:00","id":1324022,"title":"","content":"I've found that M20 summed up something about Focus/Paradigm that I've been doing for awhile and it's worked well: More useful paradigms out compete less useful paradigms even in the Traditions.<br /> <br /> Humans have always been rather flexible in their beliefs and been willing to adjust them (sometimes slowly) when it becomes untenable not to. We put so many loopholes in our societal belief structures that there's very little you can't justify doing if you twist the logic just right.<br /> <br /> The Order of Reason rose to power by disposing of the idea that magic is somehow for the chosen elite to lord over normal folks, and splintered from the Order of Hermes to bring magical power to the mundane and give it to the masses. This was useful because it gave them a resource their enemies didn't have and allowed them to survive and then overcome. The Traditions chose to abandon being strict traditionalists and adopt belief systems that viewed paradigms as individual journeys to the same end state. This created a group narrative that all magical practices come from a neutral equality and only the morality of use and wisdom of enlightenment tempers, and those the Traditions can function as a single entity against the Technocracy despite their wildly disparate ideals and practices.<br /> <br /> Being M20 made this case, I already stopped worrying about &quot;the purple paradigm&quot; (a concept I think is dumb anyway) or using paradigms as sticks. Debates and arguments about whether a mage can't do this, or can't do that, or at least needs to do X first, but no Y first, or either... it's not fun and it's not the actual point of the game.<br /> <br /> Magical style should be a carrot. It <b>is</b> a carrot in the system. Highlight this, make it clear that the more the players take their characters' magical styles into account when describing what and how they're doing it, the more bonuses they get thrown their way, rather than focusing on using paradigm as a stick to deny people things. Use it as a spectrum and let players have some fun taking risks with penalties for stretching beyond their character's norms rather than coming down with the Paradigm Hammer<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T13:04:59-07:00","id":1324039,"title":"","content":"Per what Cadmiumcadmium said, the Sphere system is great but it's important to emphasize Paradigm from the very beginning, and teach it to players that way. Otherwise they just see the open magic system and think they can do anything, which isn't exactly true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T20:25:13-07:00","id":1324122,"title":"","content":"I love the freeform style, to me, the more you can customize something, the better. And it is incredible how it can make sense in-game. My only problem with it is that sometimes it can be contradictory. Bur I guess this could be avoided by the authors, so it isn't something intrinsic to the freeform system.<br /> <br /> Also, I have no problem with the purple paradigm or with mages being able to do anything. They're already limited by their dots somehow. And if you are creative, any paradigm can cast any effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-27T17:00:04-07:00","id":1344095,"title":"","content":"Generally, I like it. In my experience the big thing is to find/convince players about the importance of paradigm and accepting that it limits what PC's can actually do with their powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-27T21:48:15-07:00","id":1344124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TacoTuesday</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1323785-sphere-system#post1323785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just curious as to how many people here actually enjoy using Mage's open toolkit. Do most here view it as a genuine pleasure or something that's a necessary evil when playing a Mage game? How does it stack up against the more defined parameters of disciplines, Gifts, and hedge sorcery? Do you find it easier or more convenient to use? I've read a lot of Mage fluff to be sure, but have never played a game with a system like this before; and in truth am a little intimidated by not having firmer guidelines in place.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does what it needs to do. Compared to the things you listed, powers from other oWoD games, MtA is far superior. It is the only WoD game I have any interest in, and it fascinates me with the possibilities.<br /> <i>However</i><br /> It is flawed. And it is a necessary evil if you want to encompass, in a single rules system, a multitude of magical styles and traditions all operating in a modern day setting. But the game is two-thirds fluff. It could use far less fluff and far more structure. There is comfort in rules. I like to bend and rewrite rules, but structure makes that easier.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25651-marko-markoko","name":"Marko Markoko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25651_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-27T22:31:18-07:00","id":1344129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1323785-sphere-system?p=1324022#post1324022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've found that M20 summed up something about Focus/Paradigm that I've been doing for awhile and it's worked well: More useful paradigms out compete less useful paradigms even in the Traditions.<br /> <br /> Humans have always been rather flexible in their beliefs and been willing to adjust them (sometimes slowly) when it becomes untenable not to. We put so many loopholes in our societal belief structures that there's very little you can't justify doing if you twist the logic just right.<br /> <br /> The Order of Reason rose to power by disposing of the idea that magic is somehow for the chosen elite to lord over normal folks, and splintered from the Order of Hermes to bring magical power to the mundane and give it to the masses. This was useful because it gave them a resource their enemies didn't have and allowed them to survive and then overcome. The Traditions chose to abandon being strict traditionalists and adopt belief systems that viewed paradigms as individual journeys to the same end state. This created a group narrative that all magical practices come from a neutral equality and only the morality of use and wisdom of enlightenment tempers, and those the Traditions can function as a single entity against the Technocracy despite their wildly disparate ideals and practices.<br /> <br /> Being M20 made this case, I already stopped worrying about &quot;the purple paradigm&quot; (a concept I think is dumb anyway) or using paradigms as sticks. Debates and arguments about whether a mage can't do this, or can't do that, or at least needs to do X first, but no Y first, or either... it's not fun and it's not the actual point of the game.<br /> <br /> Magical style should be a carrot. It <b>is</b> a carrot in the system. Highlight this, make it clear that the more the players take their characters' magical styles into account when describing what and how they're doing it, the more bonuses they get thrown their way, rather than focusing on using paradigm as a stick to deny people things. Use it as a spectrum and let players have some fun taking risks with penalties for stretching beyond their character's norms rather than coming down with the Paradigm Hammer</div> </div> </div> </div>This. In my campaigns, the \u201cpurple paradigm\u201d is merely the Traditions' unifying narrative (also known as \u201cWe Are Gods In Disguise\u201d in the Book of Secrets), and is <i>not</i> a fundamental truth of the setting; the Technocracy has its own competing unifying narrative (\u201cTech Holds All Answers\u201d) which is at odds with the Traditions' shared worldview but is no less valid. The actual truth of the setting is\u2026 up to the Storyteller. In one campaign, I may decide that the Traditions have it right and that \u201cwe <i>are</i> gods in disguise\u201d; in another, I may decide that tech does indeed hold all answers. In yet another, they may both be wrong \u2014 or both right, in a \u201cblind men and the elephant\u201d sort of way, with the actual truth being largely irrelevant. (This last one is the one I use by default.)<br /> <br /> And yes; paradigm should be a carrot. It tends to be thought of as a stick because the earlier editions described the increase in Arete as a gradual abandonment of paradigm, thus implicitly framing it as training wheels at best and a hindrance to Ascension at worst. I, too, prefer M20's approach where increased Arete doesn't liberate you from your Paradigm; it gives you a deeper understanding of it, and through its subtleties the ability to do things with it that your earlier, more naive self would have thought impossible. <br /> <br /> Though really, none of this has much to do with the Sphere System itself, other than the fact that the Spheres should <i>always</i> be handled through Focus, never <i>just</i> as Spheres. The Spheres are what you can do; your Focus is how and why you do it (Practice is the how, Paradigm is the why).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 10-28-2019, 01:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-27T22:33:12-07:00","id":1344130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cadmiumcadamium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1323785-sphere-system?p=1323945#post1323945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally prefer the Foundation and pillar system (even if i think it could use a revision) as it somewhat keeps the openness of the sphere system but each &quot;Tradition&quot; is limited by their 4 Pillars, which are specially crafted to deal with that particular mages world-view and paradigm.</div> </div> </div> </div>How would you revise it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-27T23:07:58-07:00","id":1344135,"title":"","content":"Wait, I forgot to add that I've removed Entropy. While some have argued that it thematically does something, mechanically it does very little that is actually unique, and therefore I've just removed it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/770459-entropy-sphere-mortality-decay-and-probability\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/770459-entropy-sphere-mortality-decay-and-probability\"> Entropy Sphere: Mortality/Decay and...Probability? - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/770459-entropy-sphere-mortality-decay-and-probability\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/770459-entropy-sphere-mortality-decay-and-probability </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Hey-o; newcomer to Mage here. So I've been reading through the M20 book (and discovering that despite the +700 page word count, in terms of the bare basic, need-to-know of the rules, there isn't THAT much to keep track of) and naturally, wrapping my head around its iconic magick rules and the Sphere </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/390220-is-the-sphere-of-entropy-redundant\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/390220-is-the-sphere-of-entropy-redundant\"> Is the sphere of Entropy redundant? - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/390220-is-the-sphere-of-entropy-redundant\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/390220-is-the-sphere-of-entropy-redundant </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> As the topic says, is the sphere of entropy actually needed in the game? Does it just step on the toes of other spheres? Specifically what can Entropy do is not </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T07:49:13-07:00","id":1344189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1323785-sphere-system?p=1344130#post1344130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would you revise it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would for example make sure that all Fellowships are pretty much balanced (and nerf Wise One like hell). I mostly speaking from a OoH view where it seems that anything a Hermetic can do another Fellowship can do, and better (except for creating Talismans).<br /> <br /> Also, i would make sure that the Pillars the OoH have would allow them to Summon/Control/Ward against and do pacts with Umbral entities without bending the system backwards to explain it as an afterthought.<br /> <br /> My view is that Dark Ages Mage gave OoH pretty much their corresponding Spheres (Life, Mind, Prime and Forces) and then made sure that each and every one of the other Fellowships were better, cooler and stronger than them. But that may just be my personal opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T19:07:01-07:00","id":1344322,"title":"","content":"I like the freeform aspects of Mage too, but I also like Dark Age: Mage's approach because of its differences (a different 'route' to the same end) and because I see it as an intermediate step between linear magic and dynamic (sphere) magic. Sphere magic is the current evolution of magical theory and perhaps its most 'elemental' (if you pardon the term.) It might be something that is taught by the Traditions or Technocracy (their onw particular flavors) but you could see other approaches to magic still applying (Foundations and Pillars having ties to Linear magic in my mind make it a great way to explain Orphan powers.) <br /> <br /> I'm also fond of the Storyteller handbook's 'optional' rules for Mage for much that same reason (it offers different ways to approach the same idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T22:37:26-07:00","id":1344351,"title":"","content":"I am not a fan of Dark Ages magic. Ars Magica is a far superior rules system for that specific era of history. It is both more well defined, and the definitions make it far easier if you want to &quot;free-form&quot; it. But that system doesn't work well in a modern time frame, and everything is strictly defined by an Aristotelian/Hermetic Paradigm (one that is far different from Mage, and serves as the default physical laws of the mundane world). And it is a very complex game. The advantage of Mage and Spheres is simplicity. WoD games are much easier to start up and create characters. The Sphere magic system, which does require some self discipline on the player's part, it is easy to bend it to make it emulate whatever you are imagining.<br /> <br /> I do not want to revert to anything as rigid as old AD&amp;D or tap cards for mana. I would prefer a tad bit more structure, but M20 is structured well enough that I can work with it. I am looking into some of the ideas presented in Awakening. I am not into the setting so much, but I admit that is because it is unfamiliar (and I am HermesFlambeau fanatic). But I am into some of the structured elements. Not all of them. I prefer the Spheres. I am just keen on the idea of having an advantage in leaning and using specific Rotes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25651-marko-markoko","name":"Marko Markoko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25651_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T13:46:56-07:00","id":1345046,"title":"","content":"It's nice, but I do know one st who had problems wrapping his head around it. In the end he capped arete at 2, and sphere ratings at 1 and just had us run as mage students.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8754-corioliseffect","name":"CoriolisEffect","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T14:11:34-07:00","id":1345054,"title":"","content":"Not to bash your game but that sounds kinda boring. Sphere rating 1 basically means no one can /do/ much of anything. It's all perception, no one is out here manipulating a damn thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-01T22:32:04-07:00","id":1345387,"title":"","content":"&gt;stirs and shifts in sarcophagus&lt; <br /> <br /> &gt;opens eyes&lt;<br /> <br /> *****<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cadmiumcadamium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1323785-sphere-system?p=1344189#post1344189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I would for example make sure that all Fellowships are pretty much balanced (and nerf Wise One like hell). I mostly speaking from a OoH view where it seems that anything a Hermetic can do another Fellowship can do, and better (except for creating Talismans).</div> </div> </div> </div>What about Wise One do you feel needs to be nerfed? (Not agreeing or disagreeing, just wondering...)<br /> Also, what do you perceive as other Fellowships being &quot;better&quot; at doing than the OoH, relative to the latter's designated emphasized areas? (Nobody manipulates (L)ife as well as they do, relative to having it all available in one Pillar; despite some contextual competition from the Spirit Talkers, their use of Prim(e/us) is unparalleled relative to manipulating magical energies (especially being able to extract Quintessence from objects/beings, including (de/re)-transubstantiating objects into raw (P)ower); they can more directly manipulate energies/momentum, in toto, than any other group (The Old Faith has those qualities spread across their Pillars, while others only reflect a slice of the pie relative to a given set of examples, such as The Valdaermen being able to manifest fire/cold with Hjaldar:3, but a Hermetic being able to control such more directly with Vires as well as manifest a full array of energies at that level); and only a Batini comes close, via Al-Fatihah, to matching Corona's mind/astral-related powers -- all others fall far short. I don't see the issue -- the specific combo of Pillars assigned to the OoH (especially when Materia is added) has several &quot;money-shots&quot; of its own that the other fellowships don't readily match except via more effort (conjunctional magic and likely Quintessence and Willpower), though of course there are a number of things that are equally true in reverse.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cadmiumcadamium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1323785-sphere-system?p=1344189#post1344189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, i would make sure that the Pillars the OoH have would allow them to Summon/Control/Ward against and do pacts with Umbral entities without bending the system backwards to explain it as an afterthought.</div> </div> </div> </div>They can already do that well enough with Astral entities via Corona; add Primus (that is, a conjunctional effect, the same as how some other groups have to do similarly to accomplish &quot;x&quot;, &quot;y&quot; or &quot;z&quot; relative to their paradigms) and they have limited-but-adequate (as intended) ability to do that with Middle and Low Umbral entities (and such can be warded against with Corona and/or Primus, alone, though via different results). It doesn't require any more &quot;bending backwards&quot; than with any other group; I thought it was quite easy to discern even before finishing the book when it came out almost 20 years ago, and the Grimoire did a decent job of &quot;cleaning up&quot; what albeit-should-have-been-in-the-main-book-to-begin-with examples.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cadmiumcadamium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1323785-sphere-system?p=1344189#post1344189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My view is that Dark Ages Mage gave OoH pretty much their corresponding Spheres (Life, Mind, Prime and Forces) and then made sure that each and every one of the other Fellowships were better, cooler and stronger than them. But that may just be my personal opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>That may be because the OoH's Pillars are metaphysically more in-sync with the mechanics of the pre-existing Sphere system, and therefore consequently <i>seem </i>&quot;less magical&quot; than the other Foundation/Pillar sets, but they cover essentially as much ground as the others do but in a more focused context vs say the OF's &quot;shotgun pattern&quot; of metaphysics relative to the Seasons (wherein trying to simulate what the OoH can do in one of their Pillars requires considerable understanding/ability across *all* of the OF's Pillars -- such as with Vires, for example, wherein an OF witch would have to have all the seasons at 3 in order to do what the OoH wizard can with Vires:3... and the wizard will still be able to control/transmute/conjure many manifestations of energy better than the witch because he does so with less effort/difficulty (lower DC's because only one Pillar involved, plus possibly lower DCs even further due to being able to have Vires be a Pillar covered by their second dot of Foundation, again meaning less effort than on the witch's part).<br /> <br /> I think you just have to turn the dial on the kaleidoscope another notch or two and the focus of the OoH will shine a bit clearer relative to the other Fellowships....<br /> <br /> *****<br /> <br /> &gt;eyelids slowly close&lt; &gt;shifts in sarcophagus&lt;<br /> <br /> &gt;returns to dormant state&lt;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-01T23:28:50-07:00","id":1345397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jihelu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1323785-sphere-system?p=1345054#post1345054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to bash your game but that sounds kinda boring. Sphere rating 1 basically means no one can /do/ much of anything. It's all perception, no one is out here manipulating a damn thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see it as a different style of Mage game. You know, the whole Street Level Mage games Revised worked so hard to make the default. Where the characters start as scarcely more potent than your average Sleeper, and thus need to rely on their mundane abilities (as <i>informed</i> by supernatural senses) to solve problems.<br /> <br /> Yes, I am a fan of the fantastical, but being more grounded doesn't make something boring. It could be pretty challenging, since the PCs can rely on magick to solve all their problems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-03T04:43:46-08:00","id":1345573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jihelu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1323785-sphere-system?p=1345054#post1345054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to bash your game but that sounds kinda boring. Sphere rating 1 basically means no one can /do/ much of anything. It's all perception, no one is out here manipulating a damn thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh it was tons of funs. We travelled trough the umbra(trough portals or due to more powerful beings than us flinging us into the place), to horizon realms, to shard realms, once trough time, fought vampires, talked to vampires, flirted with vampires, talked with daemons saved our teachers (they got into a lot of trouble), went to a verbena party, or just out on town, had seekings, fought the tradition bureocracy, fought an elite team of technocratic students (who coincidentally seemed to have a similar yet inverted thematic to our characters I wonder why), one of us dated one of them, we got high, my character learnt a bit of do, one guy learnt medicine(verbena), one of the npc students got pretty decent at tradition law, we participated in a large battle against a wyld behemoth, one of the player characters murdered his aunt with a rock(it was a special rock - the one Cain used to murder Abel - he gave it back to the hermetic he'd got it from afterwards), we interacted with individual traditions, i think the most common traditions in the campaign where the hermetics, verbana and chorists, then the etherites, euthanatoi, virtual adepts, then the akashics and ecstatics. I know we travelled to one of the verban strongholds, and also one of the chorist strong holds at different occasions. Got a hold of a few dangerous wonders and artifacts, though not a lot.<br /> <br /> Also lots of homework and practice.<br /> <br /> Oh also lots of travels. Homebase in england, then for various adventures we went to france, america, the armenian desert, sweden, america once. Usually either trough uncontrolled teleportation, gate network, master, or not uncommonly; roadtrip. That's of course in addition to all the off world travel.<br /> <br /> I made the verbena Primus cry tears of laughter the one time I met her. Also the st. Good times.<br /> <br /> Um. It wasn't extremely street level. But it was fun!<br /> <br /> He didn't cap the sphere levels entirely at 1 though, it was just if we wanted to do a higher level spell it needed to be something limited and we needed to spend a lot of time learning it. I think two or three people managed to get something at a higher level.<br /> <br /> In a prior mage campaign before this one we played as archmasters, with a different gm. The gm for this one was probably inspired by that one and wanted both to limit the effects a bit and run the opposite type of game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8754-corioliseffect","name":"CoriolisEffect","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T10:09:51-08:00","id":1347273,"title":"","content":"Games that limit you also offer opportunities to be more creative in how you apply using magic since you have fewer ways to 'brute force' your way through things. Sort of Mage: The Macguyvering I think. There's always an appeal to that kind of puzzle solving the same way trying to figure out creative ways to get the best milage out of level one disciplines/gifts/etc can be. It's the same sort of challenge that make different approaches to most systems do (including Dark Age Mage. Part of why I mentioned that is BECAUSE it is more limiting in many ways, but also reflects a different way to approach magic. For example with the Order of Heremes I've sometimes thought of it as a good way to represent 'theurgia' - an interim step between sorcery and sphere magic.)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T19:45:36-08:00","id":1348120,"title":"","content":"I actually really do like the Sphere system, but as a roleplayer first and foremost I hate the purple paradigm and the troubles it brings when playing with someone who is trying to powergame. It /is/ much simpler to run than the Foundations and Pillars. <br /> That said I love the Foundations and Pillars of DA:M the most. I love the thematic-ness of it, and the creative challenge it creates. It really eliminates the presence of the purple paradigm powergame by baking a countermeasure into its mechanics. Lorewise the Foundations and Pillars make much more sense to me than the Sphere System.<br /> In the end use which one you like, but my advice would be, really only play Mage with people you know, like, and know how they play. Otherwise Mage will just make everyone crazy and/or angry. Its definitely a game where everyone at your table really needs to be on the same page otherwise its not going to be fun for anyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25226-knightfenrirwulfhart","name":"KnightFenrirWulfhart","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T04:15:32-08:00","id":1348210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KnightFenrirWulfhart</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1323785-sphere-system?p=1348120#post1348120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but as a roleplayer first and foremost I hate the purple paradigm and the troubles it brings when playing with someone who is trying to powergame.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mmmh, depending on the kind of game, it is pretty much the ST's job to vet the characters during character generation. A character who tries to purple paradigm everything pretty much circumvents a lot of the balancing mechanics that Mage tries to bring to the table, as Mage HEAVILY relies on the player putting self-restraints on their chacter. Their human beliefs, their magickal paradigm, moral code, or simply believing that they *can't* do certain things, period. Another reason why I am glad that M20 makes the point that, even if mages tend to drop a lot of instrument, their paradigm tends to stay in their heads.<br /> <br /> Now, the purple paradigm can be a much stronger problem in certain types of online games where the character generation is much more freeform, with less of an ST direction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}